----ENDF/B-VII        MATERIAL 4400                               4400 1451    7
-----ATOMIC RELAXATION DATA                                       4400 1451    8
------ENDF-6 FORMAT                                               4400 1451    9
==================================================================4400 1451   10
The Livermore Evaluated Atomic Data Library (EADL) in the         4400 1451   11
ENDF-6 Format. Translated from the Livermore ENDL format          4400 1451   12
to the ENDF-6 Format by Bob MacFarlane (Los Alamos).              4400 1451   13
==================================================================4400 1451   14
  Contents                                                        4400 1451   15
==================================================================4400 1451   16
  MF/MT    Description                                            4400 1451   17
==================================================================4400 1451   18
  28/533   Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons       4400 1451   19
==================================================================4400 1451   20
  Warning                                                         4400 1451   21
==================================================================4400 1451   22
  MF/MT combinations used to define ALL electron interaction data 4400 1451   23
  are newly defined MF/MT numbers for ENDF/B-VI that did not exist4400 1451   24
  in earlier versions of ENDF/B.                                  4400 1451   25
==================================================================4400 1451   26
  Definition of Data                                              4400 1451   27
==================================================================4400 1451   28
  Atomic Relaxation Data for Electrons and Photons                4400 1451   29
==================================================================4400 1451   30
1) An atom can be ionized by a photon or an electron interaction. 4400 1451   31
2) The atomic relaxation data included here describes how a       4400 1451   32
   singly ionized atom returns to neutrality, by emitting photons 4400 1451   33
   (x-rays) and/or electrons (Auger, Coster-Kronig).              4400 1451   34
3) Data is given to define the transition probabilities between   4400 1451   35
   subshells for radiative (x-ray emission) and non-radiative     4400 1451   36
   (Auger, Coster-Kronig) transitions.                            4400 1451   37
4) The complete spectrum of emitted photons and electrons can be  4400 1451   38
   calculated using the data included here, e.g., see ref. 2,     4400 1451   39
   below, for am example of a computer code that analytically     4400 1451   40
   calculates these spectra.                                      4400 1451   41
==================================================================4400 1451   42
  References                                                      4400 1451   43
==================================================================4400 1451   44
1) S.T. Perkins, D.E. Cullen, etal., "Tables and Graphs of Atomic 4400 1451   45
   Subshell and Relaxation Data Derived from the LLNL Evaluated   4400 1451   46
   Atomic Data Library (EADL), Z = 1 - 100", UCRL-50400, Vol. 30, 4400 1451   47
   Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (1991).                 4400 1451   48
2) D.E. Cullen "Program RELAX: A Code Designed to Calculate X-Ray 4400 1451   49
   and Electron Emission Spectra as Singly Charged Atoms Relax    4400 1451   50
   Back to Neutrality", UCRL-ID-110438, Lawrence Livermore        4400 1451   51
   National Laboratory (1992).                                    4400 1451   52
                                                                  4400 1451   53
  These are the primary references to the contents of this library4400 1451   54
  and they contain a complete list of references to the sources   4400 1451   55
  of data used in this library, methods of evaluation, accuracy   4400 1451   56
  of the data, etc.                                               4400 1451   57
==================================================================4400 1451   58
  History                                                         4400 1451   59
==================================================================4400 1451   60
 (1) November, 1991 - Initial release in the ENDL format.         4400 1451   61
 (2) October,  2001 - Initial release in the ENDF-6 format.       4400 1451   62
